    <div id="tab-problem" class="tab-content">
        <h2 class="section-title">1. Problem Definition</h2>
        
        <h3 class="subsection-title">1.1 What is going wrong</h3>
        <p>Across the Dispatch & Track-and-Trace process, agents are being audited against three critical categories tied to the pickup-confirmation and TMS-update workflow. Two of the three categories—Compliance Critical (98.0%) and Customer Critical (95.8%)—are performing at or near typical operational targets (&ge; 95%). The third, Business Critical Accuracy, is materially underperforming at an 87.1% period average, with a low point of 58% and 21 individual audit days below the 80% mark.</p>
        <p>Business Critical attributes measure whether agents captured the correct pickup date/ready time in the TMS, applied the correct TMS status (Pickup Confirmed/Exception), and applied the correct accessorial code (liftgate, appointment, etc.). Because these attributes directly feed the On-Time Pickup (OTP) and On-Time Delivery (OTD) KPIs, errors here do not stay contained to an audit score—they propagate into missed pickups, re-tenders, and ultimately the customer experience, which is confirmed by the strong statistical correlation with CSAT documented in Section 3.</p>

        <h3 class="subsection-title">1.2 For how long / how far it extends</h3>
        <div class="card-grid">
            <div class="card">
                <h4>Duration</h4>
                <p>The shortfall has been present for the full 3-month audit window on record (Oct 1 - Dec 31, 2025), but it is heavily front-loaded—October is the worst month (79.9% average, with the 4 lowest single-day scores in the entire dataset).</p>
            </div>
            <div class="card">
                <h4>Scope</h4>
                <p>2,043 Business Critical interactions were audited in the period; 257 failed (12.6% fail rate), versus a 2.2% fail rate for Compliance and a 4.3% fail rate for Customer Critical over the same volume.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="card">
                <h4>Concentration</h4>
                <p>Failures are not evenly spread across shifts. Shift 3 carries the lowest Business Critical Accuracy (81.2%) versus Shift 1 (90.5%) and Shift 2 (88.6%), despite handling a similar audit volume (680 vs. 641 and 722 respectively).</p>
            </div>
            <div class="card">
                <h4>Trajectory</h4>
                <p>The metric is improving—a statistically significant upward trend of roughly +0.22 accuracy points per day (~1.5 points/week) is present in the data—but as of the December close it still sits 3.0 points below Compliance and remains the most volatile of the three categories day-to-day.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

