        <h3 class="subsection-title">3.4 What could be influencing the behavior?</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Failure type:</strong> "Missed Pickup Status" is the single largest driver, responsible for 130 of 257 Business Critical failures (50.6%).</li>
            <li><strong>Shift coverage:</strong> Shift 3 has the lowest accuracy (82.4%) and, in October specifically, produced 42 of that month's 80 "Missed Pickup Status" failures (52.5%) despite auditing only ~33% of that month's volume—a disproportionate concentration suggesting a staffing, training, or supervision gap on that shift.</li>
            <li><strong>Ramp/Training Curve:</strong> Steady month-over-month improvement is consistent with a training or coaching intervention taking hold or new hires moving up the learning curve.</li>
            <li><strong>Day-of-week effect:</strong> Accuracy is modestly lower on Fridays and Saturdays (~84-86%) than midweek (~87-91%), but the gap is small.</li>
        </ul>

