        <h3 class="subsection-title">4.2 Root cause statement</h3>
        <p>The primary root cause of the Business Critical Accuracy shortfall is inconsistent application of the correct TMS pickup status ("Pickup Confirmed" vs. "Exception") when a carrier is late or a pickup window is missed. This single failure mode drives half of all Business Critical failures and is concentrated on Shift 3 during October, indicating a shift-specific knowledge or process-adherence gap at the start of the audit window rather than a systemic tooling issue.</p>
        <p><strong>Contributing (secondary) causes (~49% of failures):</strong></p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Wrong Ready Time captured in the TMS (26.1% of failures):</strong> Suggests inconsistent confirmation of ready times with the shipping warehouse before logging.</li>
            <li><strong>Wrong Accessorial applied (23.3% of failures):</strong> Spiked in November (34 failures, up from 19 in October) before falling sharply in December (7), suggesting a temporary process or system change that was later corrected.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Because the same three reason-codes and Shift-3 concentration repeat month over month, the pattern points to a knowledge/adherence gap that responds to coaching and reinforcement.</p>
